This is a sample article about building for a small audience.

## Start with what the reader needs

An article needs a durable address, a readable layout, and a way to find the next thing. Serving a finished HTML document is a straightforward way to deliver all three.

A useful test is to open a post on a narrow screen or with scripts disabled. You should still be able to read it from beginning to end and follow its links.
